<title>USA: USTR sugar tariff-rate quota increases by country.</title>
<headline>USTR sugar tariff-rate quota increases by country.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Trade Representative's Office on Tuesday announced country-by-country additions to the fiscal year 1997 tariff-rate import quota for raw cane sugar as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>ALLOCATIONS:   Previous Additional  New FY'97</p>
<p> Argentina	 69,774	8,731     78,505</p>
<p> Australia	134,681     16,853    151,533</p>
<p> Barbados	  11,359	    0     11,359</p>
<p> Belize	    17,849	2,234     20,083</p>
<p> Bolivia	   12,981	1,624     14,606</p>
<p>ALLOCATIONS:   Previous  Additional  New FY'97</p>
<p> Brazil	   235,286     29,442    264,727</p>
<p> Colombia	  38,944	4,873     43,817</p>
<p> Congo		7,258	    0	7,258</p>
<p> Costa Rica	24,340	3,046     27,386</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	7,258	    0	7,258</p>
<p> Dom.Repub.     285,588     35,736    321,324</p>
<p> Ecuador	   17,849	2,234     20,083</p>
<p> El Salvador     42,189	5,279     47,468</p>
<p> Fiji		14,604	1,827     16,431</p>
<p> Gabon		7,258	    0	7,258</p>
<p>ALLOCATIONS:  Previous  Additional  New FY'97</p>
<p> Guatemala	 77,888	9,746     87,634</p>
<p> Guyana	    19,472	2,437     21,908</p>
<p> Haiti		7,258	    0	7,258</p>
<p> Honduras	  16,227	2,030     18,257</p>
<p> India	     12,981	1,624     14,606</p>
<p> Jamaica	   17,849	2,234     20,083</p>
<p> Madagascar	 7,258	    0	7,258</p>
<p> Malawi	    16,227	2,030     18,257</p>
<p> Mauritius	 19,472	2,437     21,908</p>
<p> Mexico	    25,000	    0     25,000</p>
<p>ALLOCATIONS:  Previous  Additional  New FY'97</p>
<p> Mozambique	21,095	2,640     23,734</p>
<p> Nicaragua	 34,076	4,264     38,340</p>
<p> Panama	    47,057	5,888     52,945</p>
<p> Pap.NewGuinea    7,258	    0	7,258</p>
